This is a demonstration for the usage of [fluvo](https://github.com/GetFluvo/fluvo) and https://github.com/GetFluvo/addons

Choosing the right branch (one branch per Odoo version)
=======================================================
This repository is organised with one branch per Odoo major version. Check out
the branch that matches the version of the Odoo server you are importing into:

    11.0           -> Odoo 11 (this branch)
    18.0 (default) -> Odoo 18
    19.0           -> Odoo 19 (uses the json2 protocol with an API key)

    git checkout 11.0   # for an Odoo 11 server (this branch)
    git checkout 18.0   # for an Odoo 18 server (default)
    git checkout 19.0   # for an Odoo 19 server

Installation
============
0) Install fluvo: `pip install fluvo` (or `uv pip install fluvo`)
1) Create an odoo 11 database named "load" with sale_management, import_metadata, import_res_id and purchase installed
2) Create users with name and login Thibault and Francois
3) activate the following lang French (BE) / Français (BE), English, Dutch / Nederlands

Your are good to go

Test
====

sh transform.sh
sh load.sh

The transform scripts generate the `fluvo import` load commands.

You've all your data into your database
